{
 "version": 1,
 "concurrency": 1,
 "jobs": [
  {
   "id": "locallane",
   "agent": "auto",
   "prompt": "Owner priority ('swarm is the builder'): add a LOCAL lane for any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint, so local models are our cheapest workers. (1) New agent name 'local' in the lane/agent registries (tools/lanes.mjs, tools/router.mjs, tools/api-adapters.mjs, tools/cli-adapters.mjs or wherever agents are enumerated; follow how 'openrouter' and 'ollama' are wired: doctor, validate, cost = 0 USD, tokens counted, usage recorded, output cap, review/test/docs/diagnose jobs allowed, build jobs that edit files only through the same single-request output path the other API lanes use). (2) Endpoints are configured in project/machine config under lanes.local.endpoints = [{ name, baseUrl, model, slots, keychain: {service, account} }], never a key in config or in a manifest or log. The key is read at call time from the macOS Keychain (service 'project-swarm', account like 'local.dev2'; use the same secure-read helper the anthropic lane uses; on Linux an env var named in config), sent as Authorization: Bearer, never printed or recorded, never reaches a worker prompt. A job selects an endpoint with model 'local:<name>' or the router picks the first healthy one. (3) Concurrency: per-endpoint slot cap from config (dev2 Strata = 3 slots) and a separate hard cap lanes.local.agencyConcurrency default 1 for jobs of type diagnose/test/docs run from agency/other-people calls, so we never starve the shared server; the lane scheduler must respect both. (4) Health: `swarm doctor local` does GET /v1/models with a 5 s timeout through the configured baseUrl (baseUrl may be a localhost SSH-tunnel port such as http://127.0.0.1:18000 or a tailnet address), reports model name, latency and slot count, and never hangs. Document the tunnel command in docs (ssh -N -L 18000:127.0.0.1:8000 <dev2>) and the Keychain command the owner runs: security add-generic-password -s project-swarm -a local.dev2 -w (owner runs it; the swarm never creates keys). (5) Ship with NO endpoint configured by default (the owner registers dev2 after confirming). Tests: config validation (rejects a key in config), key read injected, request shape (OpenAI chat completions, stream off, temperature low), usage mapping, slot cap and agencyConcurrency, doctor timeout, key never appears in logs/errors (grep the error paths), router skips an unhealthy endpoint. No real network or Keychain in tests. Keep existing lane/router tests passing. IMPORTANT (a previous attempt was blocked by the repo's secret-scan security gate at integrate): test fixtures must NEVER contain anything that looks like a secret assignment (no `apiKey: 'something'`, `key = '...'`, `token: '...'`, long random-looking strings, or keys that start with sk-). Use fake key values that are built at runtime from parts (for example ['fake','local','value'].join('-')) assigned to variables whose names do not contain key, secret, token or password, or read them from the injected readKey function, and assert redaction by checking that the runtime value does not appear in logs and errors. Run the repo's secret scan on your test file (tools has a secret-scan module; find it with grep) and make sure it reports nothing.",
   "context": [
